    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Croix-Valmer and Bormes-les-Mimosas offer several campsites and rentals that accept dogs, including holiday villages with equipped mobile homes. A good compromise between the quiet of the area and proximity to Cavalaire-sur-Mer.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>Note: the dog beach in La Croix-Valmer, which existed in 2017, was removed by the town hall as early as 2018. For swimming, you'll therefore need to head to Cavalaire-sur-Mer or Bormes-les-Mimosas instead.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: it's best to check the current beach rules on site, since this kind of municipal decision can change again from one season to the next.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Bonporteau beach in Cavalaire-sur-Mer, about ten minutes away, remains the most reliable swimming option in the area.</p>
